From 17a6fbc72f462edcfd62f7977d75b0c2eccd7d96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pleiades <fleagle2001@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 09:12:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] statewise v1 static MoE expert cache (Pleiades port of
 ionizedd/llama.cpp-Statewise)

Hand-ported v1 static cache onto Pleiades' vendored llama.cpp (b46812de), for the
qwen35moe (Ornith 35B-A3B) architecture. v1 only; v2 online adaptation descoped.

- ggml-cpu mul_mat_id: sentinel id (-1) => zero dst row + skip (cold-side hits).
- ggml-cuda mul_mat_id: placement tripwire (op_params[0]==1 aborts) mirroring Ion's
  vulkan tripwire; the cold, sentinel-bearing side must stay on CPU. No CUDA -1 skip
  kernel (Ion measured shader-side skip at ~11% and rejected it; cold side is CPU-owned).
- llama-graph build_moe_ffn (both overloads): decode-only (n_tokens<=8) split into a GPU
  hot chain (per-layer cache tensors, miss=>dummy zero slot) + CPU cold chain (sentinel
  ids), recombined by add. Guarded for separate gate/up, no per-expert scales/biases, SILU.
- llama-model statewise_init: load-time cache alloc/fill from LLAMA_STATEWISE_MAP profile;
  public C API llama_model_statewise_init(); env-var hook in llama.cpp for cli/bench A/B.
- qwen35moe.cpp: wire per-layer cache into the shared build_moe_ffn call.

Validated on RTX 2080 Ti + real Ornith Q6_K: test-backend-ops MUL_MAT_ID 764/764 (CPU+CUDA);
64-tok greedy output token-identical cache OFF vs ON; llama-bench tg96 18.66 -> 24.97 t/s
(+33.8%) at K=32. 256-tok run diverges at a greedy tie (~75 tok) from GPU/CPU expert
numerics - benign, same class as -ngl variation (matches Ion's ba758e0cb finding).
